#: ../../../minversions.md:24
msgid "Minimum Supported Versions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../minversions.md:26
msgid ""
"PyGMT has adopted [SPEC 0](https://scientific-python.org/specs/spec-0000/) "
"alongside the rest of the scientific Python ecosystem, and will therefore:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../minversions.md:29
msgid "Drop support for Python versions 3 years after their initial release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../minversions.md:30
msgid ""
"Drop support for core package dependencies (NumPy, pandas, xarray) 2 years "
"after their initial release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../minversions.md:33
msgid "In addition to the above, the PyGMT team has also decided to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../minversions.md:35
msgid ""
"Drop support for GMT versions 3 years after their initial release, while "
"ensuring at least two latest minor versions remain supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../minversions.md:37
msgid ""
"Maintain support for [optional dependencies](/ecosystem.md#pygmt-"
"dependencies) for at least 1 year after their initial release. Users are "
"encouraged to use the most up-to-date optional dependencies where possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../minversions.md:42
msgid ""
"The SPEC 0 policy is enforced on a best-effort basis, and the PyGMT team may "
"decide to drop support for core (and optional) package dependencies earlier "
"than recommended for compatibility reasons."
msgstr ""

